From b879a8d8be9d2767515ae67d87b3994612ea122a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CL Wang <cl634@andestech.com>
Date: Wed, 31 Jul 2024 22:41:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 056/168] dmaengine: andes: atcdmac300: Support for DMA
 operation in a multi-hart and multi-threaded environment

1. Add a new variable "chan_used" to indicate whether the DMA channel is
   in use and to restrict the DMA channel to be used by only one thread
   at a time.
2. Refine spin_lock_irqsave to lock_lock or spin_lock_bh because the
   shared resources are not used in the ISR.

Signed-off-by: CL Wang <cl634@andestech.com>
---
 drivers/dma/atcdmac300.c | 101 ++++++++++++++++++++-------------------
 drivers/dma/atcdmac300.h |   3 ++
 2 files changed, 54 insertions(+), 50 deletions(-)
 mode change 100644 => 100755 drivers/dma/atcdmac300.c

diff --git a/drivers/dma/atcdmac300.c b/drivers/dma/atcdmac300.c
old mode 100644
new mode 100755
index 7117865a1ce1..b182b148099e
--- a/drivers/dma/atcdmac300.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/atcdmac300.c
@@ -58,12 +58,11 @@ static dma_cookie_t v5_tx_submit(struct dma_async_tx_descriptor *tx)
